      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)}{xy}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)}{xy}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot (\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y)\\cdot x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)\\cdot 1}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)}{{x}^{2}y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
